\title{merkmal: phonological feature systems and segment distances}
\description{
R bindings to the merkmal C library, which maps IPA transcriptions of
speech segments to feature representations under several feature systems
and computes dissimilarities between segments. The C core is compiled into
the package; there is no system dependency.
}
\details{
Every function that reads segments takes a \code{system} (default
\code{"distinctive"}) and a \code{registry} (default: the built-in systems). The
functions are vectorized over their segment arguments. A segment that a
system cannot read gives \code{NA} with a warning, never a guessed value; use
\code{\link[=is_segment]{is_segment()}} to test and \code{\link[=diagnose]{diagnose()}} to learn why.

Results depend on the system, its version and the scoring policy. Store
\code{\link[=system_fingerprint]{system_fingerprint()}} or \code{\link[=operation_fingerprint]{operation_fingerprint()}} with any result kept.
